/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_LUTLine Line
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_LUT
 * @brief Build a normalized one-dimensional curve and inspect capacity behavior.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTLine_Goal Goal
 * Fill a five-sample curve, reserve capacity, then shrink and regrow it. The
 * tutorial makes values, size and allocation reuse observable without exposing
 * implementation storage to a consumer.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTLine_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_LUT_Line_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTLine_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * curve[0]=0%; expected=0%
 * curve[1]=25%; expected=25%
 * curve[2]=50%; expected=50%
 * curve[3]=75%; expected=75%
 * curve[4]=100%; expected=100%
 * Regrown samples=0; pointer retained; capacity=8: PASS
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * The regrowth line demonstrates that reserving eight elements allows a later
 * resize within that capacity to reuse the existing allocation.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTLine_Code Implementation
 * \include LUT/Line/Shared.cpp
 */
